# Third-Party Licenses

This file lists the third-party software used by the Liphia engine
and their respective licenses.

---

## Rust Standard Library and Toolchain

The Liphia engine (`liphia_compiler`, `liphia_virtual_machine`,
`liphia_cli`) is implemented in Rust and compiled using the Rust
toolchain.

- **Project:** The Rust Programming Language
- **Website:** https://www.rust-lang.org
- **Repository:** https://github.com/rust-lang/rust
- **License:** MIT OR Apache-2.0 (dual license)

The Rust standard library is statically linked into the Liphia
engine binary. Its use is governed by the MIT and Apache 2.0
licenses, copies of which are available at:

  - https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/master/LICENSE-MIT
  - https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/master/LICENSE-APACHE

---

## Standard Library Crates (Rust)

The following modules from the Rust standard library are used
directly in the Liphia engine source code:

| Module            | Usage                                      |
|-------------------|--------------------------------------------|
| `std::collections::HashMap` | Global variable storage in the VM  |
| `std::collections::HashSet` | Import cycle detection in the CLI  |
| `std::fs`         | Source file reading                        |
| `std::path`       | File path resolution                       |
| `std::io`         | stdin/stdout for `input` and `print`       |
| `std::rc::Rc`     | Reference-counted string values in the VM  |

All of the above are part of the Rust standard library and are
covered by the Rust license stated above.

---

## No Additional Runtime Dependencies

The Liphia engine has **no external crate dependencies** beyond
the Rust standard library. The `Cargo.toml` files contain no
entries in `[dependencies]`.

This means the compiled binary is fully self-contained and does
not bundle any third-party crates subject to separate licensing.

